==Latvian==

===Etymology 1===
A {{borrowing|liv|või|lang=lv|nocap=1}} or dialectal {{etyl|et|lv}} ''vai''; compare other {{etyl|fiu-fin|-}} languages ({{cog|fi|vai}}, Standard {{cog|et|või}}). First found occasionally in {{etyl|lv|-}} writings in the 17th century, initially as a conjunction, then as a particle, it became more frequent in the 18th century; but only in the 19th century did it really strike root in the language.<ref name="LEV">{{R:lv:LEV}}</ref>

====Pronunciation====
{{lv-IPA|vài|falling}}
{{rfap|lang=lv}}

====Conjunction====
{{head|lv|conjunction}}

# {{non-gloss definition|[[use]]d to [[indicate]] a [[disjunction]] [[between]] [[two]] [[element]]s}}; [[or]] {{gloss|in the [[either-or]] sense, not in the sense of [[a.k.a.]], which is {{m|lv|jeb}}}}.
#: ''atbildi: jā '''vai''' nē!'' — answer: yes '''or''' no!
#: ''viņa nezināja, ko pirkt: rozes '''vai''' neļķes'' — she didn't know what to buy: roses '''or''' carnations
# {{non-gloss definition|[[use]]d to [[suggest]] [[vagueness]], [[uncertainty]], or a [[veiled]] [[threat]]; [[usually]] [[follow]]ed by [[ellipsis]] (...)}}; [[or]], [[or else]]...
#: ''ja labi grib, to darbu var veikt parasts dežurants, '''vai''' brigadieris, '''vai''' (...)'' — if (he) really wants, an ordinary man on duty can do this job, '''or''' a brigadier, '''or'''... (= or someone like that)
#: ''vai tas kāds noziegums, kauns, '''vai'''''? — is this a crime, a shame, '''or what'''?
#: ''jums tas jādara, '''vai'''...'' — you all have to do this, '''or else'''...
# {{non-gloss definition|[[use]]d to [[introduce]] [[conditional]] [[subordinate clause]]s}}; [[whether]], [[if]]
#: ''nav zināms, '''vai''' to darījis viņš'' — it is not known '''whether''' he did it
#: ''es nezinu, '''vai''' to spēšu'' — I don't know '''if''' I will be able to
#: ''pasaki, '''vai''' es esmu nodevējs'' — tell me '''if''' I am a traitor

=====See also=====
* {{l|lv|jeb}}

====Particle====
{{head|lv|particle}}

# {{non-gloss definition|[[interrogative]] [[particle]], used in [[either-or]] [[question]]s}}
#: '''''vai''' tu runā latviski?'' — do you speak Latvian?
#: '''''vai''' tu dzirdi?'' — do you hear? are you listening?

====Noun====
{{lv-noun|m|-}}

# {{non-gloss definition|the [[word]] {{m|lv|vai}} [[itself]]; also, [[implicitly]], a [[question]]}}
#: ''cits pēc cita nāca tik daudzi '''vai''', ka viņa nevarēja ilgāk izturēt'' — so many '''vai''''s (= questions) came one after the other that she couldn't stand it any longer

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|ine-pro|lv}} {{m|ine-pro|*wai||suffer, be miserable}}. Cognates include {{cog|lt|vái}}, {{m|lt|vai|vaĩ}}, {{cog|goh|wē}}, {{cog|ang|wā}}, {{cog|la|vae}}, {{cog|de|weh}}, {{cog|en|woe}}.<ref name="LEV"/>

====Pronunciation====
{{lv-IPA|vāī|level}}, {{lv-IPA|vài|falling}}, {{lv-IPA|vaî|broken}} (depending on situational intonation)

====Interjection====
{{head|lv|interjection}}

# used to express emotional responses: [[excitement]], [[surprise]], [[pain]], [[fear]], [[sorrow]], [[irritation]], etc.
#: '''''vai''', ko es daru!'' — '''oh'''! what am I doing!
#: '''''vai''', kāds jūs līks izskatāties!'' — '''boy''', look at you! what a sight!
#: '''''vai''', '''vai''', Ilma, '''vai''', tev tikai nauda prātā!'' — '''oh come on''', Ilma, you only think about money!

===References===
<references />

